          "authorityIds": "col:4HVJC,wfo:wfo-0001265233",
          "description": "<div><p>3. Pilostyles hamiltonii Gardner, J. Roy. Soc. Western Australia 32: 77. 1948.</p> <p>Type.</p> <p>Australia, Western Australia, Darling District, Helena Rover, Mundaring Weir, Mar. 1946, parasitic on Daviesia pectinata Lindl., C. D. Hamilton s.n. (PERTH, not seen).</p> <p>Note: Tepals dark burgundy, in 2 whorls, flowers>3 mm in diameter. Growing in young stems of Daviesia in Western Australia (Figs 2, 3, see Thiele et al. 2008 for pictures of flowers).</p> </div>",
          "authorship": "C.A.Gardner"
        },
        {
