          "authorityIds": "col:4HVJD,wfo:wfo-0001265240",
          "description": "<div><p>6. Pilostyles haussknechtii Boissier, Arch. Sci. Phys. Nat. 25: 255-261. 1866.</p> <p>Type.</p> <p>Middle East, parasitic on Astragalus, J. E. Haussknecht s.n (G-BOISS, not seen).</p> <p>Note: Tepals pink to brown in 2 whorls, each with 6 to 10 tepals (Fig. 6G). Found at the basis of young branches of Astragalus and occasionally Onobrychis and Halimodendron in Iran (Figs 2, 3).</p> </div>"
        },
